The '''Imperial Center of Military Research''', also known as the '''Imperial security complex''' and commonly known as '''Scarif base''', was an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] research and development installation located on the tropical [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] of [[Scarif]]. The facility was the center for research, structural [[engineer]]ing, munitions and manufacturing for the [[Project Stardust|Death Star project]]. Shortly before the [[Battle of Yavin]], the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] managed to penetrate Scarif's [[deflector shield]] and launch an [[Battle of Scarif|attack]] on the security complex as part of their mission to steal the [[Death Star plans|plans]] to the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]].

==Description==
[[File:Citadel_Tower_Schematics.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Schematics of the Citadel Tower.]]
The [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] security complex was a vast installation located on the surface of the tropical<ref name="Rogue One" /> [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]<ref name="UVG" /> [[planet]] of [[Scarif]]. Consisting of a large, wide-based tower,<ref name="Rogue One" /> known as the [[Citadel Tower]],<ref name="Battlefront">''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]''</ref> surrounded by various facilities including [[hangar]] bays and barracks, the security complex was the center for research, structural [[engineer]]ing, supply storage and manufacturing for the [[Project Stardust]], a program dedicated to the construction of the Empire's planet-destroying [[battle station]], the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]. Because of its role in the program, the complex was often visited by its [[director]], [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic]] of [[Imperial Military Department of Advanced Weapons Research]]<ref name="Rogue One" /> who maintained an executive [[Hangar|landing pad]] on the Citadel Tower. For troop and supply transportation between the Tower and the planet-wide facilities, a [[train]] system comprised of spacious [[armor]]ed wagons running on reinforced tracks was installed and allowed for the safe deployment of troops to wherever they were needed in the complex.<ref name="UVG" />

==History==
[[File:ScarifDestroyed.jpg|thumb|200px|The destruction of the Imperial Center of Military Research during the Battle of Scarif.]]
Construction of the Death Star moved to the planet Scarif after its time over [[Geonosis]].<ref name="Secret Mission">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: Secret Mission]]''</ref> The facility was commanded by [[General]] [[Sotorus Ramda]]. Shortly before the [[Battle of Yavin]], the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] launched an [[Battle of Scarif|attack]] on Scarif as part of their mission to steal the [[Death Star plans|plans]] to the Death Star. After penetrating the planet's [[deflector shield]] through means of a [[Shield Gate]], the Rebel Alliance assaulted the security complex. While rebel forces waged a pitched battle against the Imperial garrison on land and space, [[Jyn Erso]] and [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] managed to transmit the plans with considerable difficulty to the rebel fleet in orbit. In a desperate attempt to prevent the rebels from escaping with the stolen Death Star plans, [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] ordered the Death Star to destroy the security complex and Scarif using its superlaser. This led to the deaths of all participants on Scarif. But despite his efforts, [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] managed to escape with the Death Star plans on the [[CR90 corvette]] ''[[Tantive IV]]'' into [[hyperspace]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Scarif_complex_concept_art.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Concept art of the Imperial security complex with the Death Star docking tower in the center.]]
The Imperial security complex was a location created and developed for the premier ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Star Wars Anthology Series|anthology film]], ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="Imperial architecture">{{SW|url=news/designing-an-empire-doug-chiang-on-imperial-architecture-in-rogue-one|text=Designing an Empire: Doug Chiang on Imperial Architecture in ''Rogue One''}}</ref> released on [[December 16]], [[2016]].<ref name="Director Announced">{{SW|url=news/gareth-edwards-and-gary-whitta-onboard-for-star-wars-stand-alone-film|text=Gareth Edwards and Gary Whitta Onboard for ''Star Wars'' Stand-Alone Film}}</ref> The first footage of the complex was shown in the ''Rogue One'' teaser trailer on [[April 7]], 2016.<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|Wji-BZ0oCwg|ROGUE ONE: A STAR WARS STORY Official Teaser Trailer}}</ref>

In early development of ''Rogue One'', the Imperial security complex was envisioned as an installation that the Death Star would dock with directly, acting as an [[Turbolift|elevator]] through which materials could be ferried to the [[battle station]] from the planet's surface. The overall shape of the facility was inspired by the data ports accessed by [[R2-D2]] in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="Imperial architecture" /> Though many aesthetic characteristics were retained for the installation's final design, the docking tower was changed to the Citadel Tower which featured a large transmission array at the summit.<ref name="Rogue One" />

